    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds the structured `OWNER_CREATED` audit event with minimal structural impact.\n\n**New file** \u2014 `util/OwnerCreatedEvent.java`: a small, cohesive class (near-zero surrounding complexity) that owns the whole feature:\n- A static `AtomicLong SEQ` gives a monotonically increasing `seq` across all creates.\n- `emit(owner, membershipLevel)` logs the immutable JSON `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event:'OWNER_CREATED'}` to the `AUDIT` logger.\n- `primaryIdentifier(Owner)` isolates *which* field is the primary identifier \u2014 today `customerCode`. When the customerCode is later unified into the memberId, only this one-liner changes and the event automatically carries the memberId instead (the JSON key stays `customerCode` per the spec, but its value follows the primary identifier).\n\n**Controller** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`: a single added line calling `OwnerCreatedEvent.emit(...)`. The large `addOwner` method and the high-WMC controller class are otherwise untouched, so the expensive lever (WMC_other \u00d7 CC \u00d7 changed_lines) is paid on just one line rather than absorbed into new branching or a grown method.\n\nThe existing plain audit line is left as-is; the structured event is emitted alongside it. Tests are green.",
